            <ArticleTitle>Barth Syndrome with Late-Onset Cardiomyopathy: A Missed Opportunity for Diagnosis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>196-198</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0022-3476(16)31565-7</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.jpeds.2016.12.070</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A male infant presented with neutropenia, growth delay, and death of a maternal uncle at age 2 years. Despite extensive evaluation over 10 years, Barth syndrome was not diagnosed until he presented in acute heart failure. Although late-onset cardiomyopathy is rare, persistence of common Barth features should have enabled earlier diagnosis.</AbstractText>
